      "body": "thermal_stability_upper_bound = 300.0 K at 1.013 bar"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "oxalate-pillared three-dimensional framework from Zn-aminotriazolate layers → unknown"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "CO2-amine interactions and small pores with overlapping attractive potentials → qst"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] use 3-amino-1,2,4-triazole to build amine-functionalized micropores in Zn-MOFs → supports selective CO2 capture at low partial pressure through high CO2 adsorption energy and uptake together with lack of uptake for other gases"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] favor amine-functionalized microporous frameworks over large-pore MOFs for low-pressure CO2 capture → improves efficiency at lower pressures"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "framework 1 vs reported related framework with different structure: winner=subject_a on porosity"
    }
